# Personal project workflow

Canonical: `docs/Personal_Rules.md` sections 1, 2, 18, and 19.

## Before implementation

- Read the root `docs` and the feature's existing wiki page.
- Reuse the confirmed local Windows desktop-game scope and Electron/Next.js/NestJS/SQL Server decisions in `docs/ProjectInfo.md`. Do not ask the owner to select that stack again or treat earlier game-design suggestions as approved scope.
- For new gameplay requirements, confirm purpose, users and roles, current and desired workflows, rules, approvals, statuses, exceptions, supported devices, success criteria, scope, languages, integrations, and authentication with the owner.
- Separate must-have, optional, future, and out-of-scope work. Record simulations, demo limitations, open questions, and requirement changes.
- Ask about missing requirements before dependent implementation. Routine technical choices within the guide may be recorded in `Assumptions.md`; material assumptions and exceptions require review.
- This project requires username/password login and English/Vietnamese localization. Reuse confirmed decisions; no deployment is added.

## Required root documentation

| File                     | Required content                                                                                                                                                                                          |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `docs/ProjectInfo.md`    | Personal Rules version, purpose, users/devices, workflows, scope, success criteria, limitations, integrations, languages/default language, authentication, open questions, and requirement change history |
| `docs/ApiEndpoints.md`   | Endpoint summary using the configurable API prefix                                                                                                                                                        |
| `docs/PagesAndRoutes.md` | Routes, screens, shared components, and confirmed language selection/locale routing                                                                                                                       |
| `docs/Database.md`       | Tables, relationships, constraints, ID prefixes/digits/capacities/examples, and schema snapshot version                                                                                                   |
| `docs/Dependencies.md`   | Additional libraries, pinned versions, and reasons                                                                                                                                                        |
| `docs/Assumptions.md`    | Technical choices, reasons, and required owner approvals                                                                                                                                                  |

Keep these documents accurate as the code changes. Root `docs` is not `backend/Docs`.

## Completion

Use the full section 18 checklist for new modules and relevant changes. At minimum:

- Confirm stack, folders, module registry, shared UI, API boundaries, naming, palette/font, and formatting follow the guide.
- Run `pnpm lint`, `pnpm format:check`, and `pnpm test` in frontend, backend, and desktop; report failures or unavailable checks accurately.
- Confirm ID capacity, paging, standard errors, `rowVer`, DTO/entity boundaries, transactions, constraints, duplicate protection, and safe SQL scripts.
- Update the single schema snapshot with schema changes. Store database timestamps through `adelaideTime.ts`.
- Confirm database-driven options, required device accessibility, languages, login, and permissions.
- Confirm meaningful service, repository integration, HTTP, frontend, regression, and critical end-to-end coverage.
- Review secrets, logs, security, external timeouts/retries, lifecycle, and any deployment-specific checks.
- Remove leftovers created by this change and preserve owner-designated holds.
- Update component/controller headers, feature wiki, API catalog, endpoint summary, Postman collection, and any affected agent instructions.
- Keep `ProjectInfo.md` accurate, review material assumptions, and provide a short README explaining how to run the project.
- Do not mark protected operations complete while required authentication is missing, or claim unrun tests and pending validations passed.

- Desktop/runtime changes also follow desktop-electron.mdc: verify real rendering, env precedence, configured/free ports, process ownership, and shutdown. Report database connection, schema/admin setup, gameplay, and installer packaging separately; mark each pending until implemented and verified.
- Instruction-only edits require version/path/pin/metadata consistency and Markdown checks; application execution and two-agent rule validation must not be inferred from those checks.
